# Exclude dev-only paths from the archive GitHub generates (codeload tarball /
# "Download ZIP"). The Claude plugin-marketplace backend ingests that archive and
# validates it in a sandbox that rejects symlinks (path-traversal) and bloated
# content. Keeping these out of the tarball fixes the marketplace sync
# `failed_content` error without touching local dev/test/Docker: real checkouts
# (git clone) ignore `export-ignore`, so the `src` symlink and the test suite
# remain available locally.
/src   export-ignore
/tests export-ignore
